## Context
Audit of inline SKILL.md code (2026-10-11): `skills/raid/SKILL.md` embeds a
25-line awk program that parses the `--- log ---` section of every `.erg` file
to count `bump` and `note verify-reroll` / `circuit-breaker` entries per ticket.
It encodes the erg log format with no test; if erg changes its log-line shape the
counts silently drop to zero and the reroll circuit-breaker never trips.

## Exit criteria
- [x] The parser lives in a script under `skills/raid/` (or `scripts/`) or as an `erg` subcommand, with output identical to the current awk on the current ticket corpus (byte-compared)
- [x] Tests cover a `bump`, a `note bump verify-reroll`, a `note circuit-breaker`, an ignored `note`, and a body line that looks like a log line
- [x] A positive control: on a fixture with known counts the script reports them, and an empty result on a non-empty log is flagged rather than printed as zero
- [x] `skills/raid/SKILL.md` calls the script instead of the inline awk
